WEBVTT

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.030
(TOYS LAUGHING)

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:22.030
KEN: All right, place your bets.
Come on, everybody.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:23.390
-Come on. Any splits?
-TWITCH: Heya. Bring it here.

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:24.550
CHUNK: All right.
KEN: Here we go.

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:25.630
Come on, horsey, come on!

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:26.790
CHUNK: Come on, turkey,
come on, turkey.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:28.230
-Gobble, gobble, baby.
-KEN: Come on, horsey.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.390
Come on, duck.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:31.150
-All right, that's it. No more bets.
-CHUNK: Come on! Right here.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:32.390
STRETCH: Let me have the duck, let
me have the duck,

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:33.470
let me have the duck!

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.150
-FARMER: Here is a duck.
-(DUCK QUACKS)

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.710
-I won!
-TWITCH: Ah, man!

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:37.910
(GROANING)

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.550
-KEN: Well, Stretch takes the round.
-You lost! (LAUGHS)

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.270
Okay, minimum bet, five Monopoly.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:43.910
-Coyote's wild.
-STRETCH: Here, here.

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:45.470
-Two greens here.
-KEN: Changing two double A's.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:47.670
Hey, what do you guys think
of the new recruits? Any keepers?

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:49.590
Oh, please! Landfill!

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.150
-Cowgirl? Dinosaur?
-Toddler fodder.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:55.070
But that space guy, he could be useful.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:58.990
He ain't the sharpest knife in the
place where they keep the knives.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:00.270
SPARKS: Neither are you, Chunk.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:01.430
(ALL CHUCKLING)

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:03.830
You got a little keeper yourself,
didn't you, Ken?

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:06.430
Hey, lay off, Twitch. Barbie's different.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:08.430
Aw, Mr. Softy over here.

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:10.590
What do you expect from a girl's toy?

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:14.510
I'm not a girl's toy! I'm not!
Why do you guys keep saying that?

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.470
Ah, all them toys are disposable.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.510
We'll be lucky if they last us a week.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:24.790
(ALL EXCLAIMING)

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.350
Well, well. Looky who we have here.

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:29.830
Let me go!

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:31.550
Take him to the libary.

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:32.710
BUZZ: No!

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:05.150
(QUIETLY) 1225 Sycamore.

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:07.630
Psst. Woody, what are you doing?

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:09.710
I gotta get outta here.

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.670
-You're leaving?
-But didn't you have fun today?

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:14.590
Well, of course I did,
more than I've had in years,

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.750
but, you see, I belong to someone else.

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:20.070
-Who's "Yid-nuh"?
-I believe it's pronounced "Yid-nay."

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:21.990
Guys, it says "Andy."

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:23.350
He's my Bonnie.

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:25.590
And he's leaving soon.
I gotta get home.

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:28.390
-Where's home?
-Elm Street. 234 Elm.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:31.710
-You guys have a map?
-We're on it, cowboy. Trixie?

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:34.190
I'll fire up the computer.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:36.350
(GRUNTING)

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.590
Unhand me, you cowards!
I demand to talk to Lotso!

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:44.430
Zip it, Buck Rogers.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.230
You don't talk to Lotso
till we say you can...

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:53.070
Ken? What's goin' on here?
Why is this toy tied up?

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.910
(STAMMERS) He got out, Lotso.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:03:01.470
"Got out"? Oh, no, no, no, no, no.
This isn't how we treat our guests.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:06.030
F-A-Oh, my Schwarz.
There you go. I'm so sorry.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:08.630
-Lotso, there's been a mistake.
-A mistake?

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.950
The children in the Caterpillar Room
are not age-appropriate

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:12.310
for me and my friends.

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:15.310
We respectfully request
a transfer to the Butterfly Room.

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:17.230
Well, request granted!

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:19.710
-But, Lotso...
-Hush now, Kenneth.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:23.150
This toy's shown initiative, leadership.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:25.310
Why, I'd say
we've found ourselves a keeper.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.310
Hear that, everyone? We got a keeper!

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:29.470
(ALL CHEERING)

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:34.310
We're calling you up
to the big leagues, son.

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:37.230
From now on,
you'll have anything you want.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:39.310
Excellent. I'll go get my friends.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:41.990
Whoa, whoa. Hold on there, boss.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.510
Those Caterpillar kids
need someone to play with.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.510
But my friends don't belong there.

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:48.590
Oh, none of us do, I agree.

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:52.110
Which is why,
for the good of our community,

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:54.670
we ask the newer toys,
the stronger ones,

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:58.470
to take on the hardships
the rest of us can't bear anymore.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:01.990
Well, I guess that makes sense.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:06.750
But I can't accept.
We're a family. We stay together.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:09.710
Family man, huh? I understand.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.990
Put him back in the timeout chair.

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:15.470
BUZZ: What are ya... Unhand me!

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.550
Bring in the Bookworm.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:19.710
(WHISTLES)

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.630
(BOOKWORM MUMBLING)

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:24.030
BOOKWORM: Ah! Here it is.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:27.190
It was filed under "Lightyear."

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:33.630
LOTSO: Let's see here.

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:36.830
"Accessories. Maintenance."
Oh. Here we go.

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:40.630
"Remove screws to access
battery compartment."

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:41.990
What are you doing?

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:43.710
Stop!

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:45.230
Let go of me! Ow!

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:48.190
"To return
your Buzz Lightyear action figure

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:50.670
"to its original factory settings..."

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.070
No!

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:54.750
"...slide the switch from Play to Demo."

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:58.510
BUZZ: Stop! No! No! No!

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:02.070
-(GASPS) What was that?
-Sounds like it came from the hall.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.750
I'll see what it was.

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.070
JESSIE: What do you see? Anything?

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:11.710
MRS. POTATO HEAD: No, just a dark
hallway and... (GASPS) Wait. Wait!

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:13.430
I see Andy!

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.270
-What?
-That's impossible.

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:17.830
No, no, I really see him. In his room.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:21.670
(GASPS) My other eye!
The one I left behind.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:28.030
This is so weird. He's packing up.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:33.390
Uh-oh. Oh, here comes Buster.
Out of the way! Get away!

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:36.390
Okay, Andy's out in the hall.

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:39.550
He's looking in the attic.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:43.030
Wait, there's Mom.
Why is he so upset?

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.790
Oh, no! Oh, this is terrible!

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:51.430
He's looking for us.
Andy's looking for us!

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.030
He's looking for us?

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:55.950
So Andy does want us.
I knew it! I just knew it!

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:58.350
I think he did mean
to put us in the attic.

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:00.150
Well, then, Woody was telling the truth.

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:02.470
-Holy cow!
-And you didn't believe him.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:04.070
Hey, you didn't believe him first!

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:07.110
Guys, we gotta... We gotta go home!

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:10.750
-Lotso!
-Hey, there.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.390
How y'all doin' this fine evenin'?

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.830
(SIGHS) Thank goodness!
Have you seen Buzz?

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:18.230
There's been a mistake. We have to go.

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:22.830
Go? Why, you just got here.
In the nick of time, too.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:25.910
We were runnin' low on volunteers
for the little ones.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:28.670
They just love new toys,
now, don't they?

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:31.750
"Love"? We've been chewed,
kicked, drooled on.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:33.790
Just look at my pocketbook!

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:35.070
Hmm.

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:39.350
Well, here's the thing, sweet potato.
You ain't leavin' Sunnyside.

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:42.670
"Sweet potato"!
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:47.590
I have over 30 accessories,
and I deserve more respect...

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.190
-Ah... That's better.
-(TOYS CHUCKLING)

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:52.750
Hey, no one takes my wife's mouth,
except me.

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.950
Give it back, you furry air freshener!

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:56.670
Come on, guys. We're goin' home.

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:57.870
Whoa there, missy.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:06:59.870
You're not goin' anywhere.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:02.830
Oh, yeah? And who's gonna stop us?

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:06.350
Buzz! You're back!

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:07.990
-Hoo-yah!
-REX: Buzz?

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.030
Hey!

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:12.390
HAMM: Look out!

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:13.870
What are you, nuts?

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:15.230
Buzz!

